# A.4 (g): appositives.
#######################

# Appositive after the subject: a VP always follows, so commas on both sides.
1	S	NP , APPOS , VP

# Appositive after the object at the end of the sentence: only one comma, the "." closes it.
# At ROOT and not VP, so nothing can come after it (no "*... , 59 years old on the desk .").
1	ROOT	NP V1 NP , APPOS .

# Several appositives in a row, separated by single commas.
1	APPOS	APPOS , APPOS

# An appositive can be a noun phrase, a canned phrase, or "who" + a verb phrase.
1	APPOS	NP
1	APPOS	59 years old
1	APPOS	who VP

# "perplexed" is also an ordinary transitive verb ("the president perplexed Sally").
1	V1	perplexed